@mainpage Documentation of the Ali Project

@section intro Introduction

This project is a 2D platform game developed in C with the SDL2 library.

It includes a volume menu, a mini-map, mobile/fragile platforms,

obstacles, background animations, and audio controls.

@section features Features

    Platform Game: Move the character with the arrow keys

    Mini-map: Reduced view of the level with pulsation

    Platforms: Fixed, horizontally/vertically mobile, fragile

    Obstacles: Block the passage

    Volume Menu: Volume control, fullscreen, mute

    Animations: Shake, flash, wave, red tint on collision

    Two Levels: Switch levels with the SPACE key

@section controls Controls

    Arrow keys: Move the character

    V: Open/Close the volume menu

    SPACE: Change level

    ESC: Exit the game

    In the volume menu: Mouse click on buttons

@section files Main files

    main.c: Program entry point

    function.c: Volume menu functions

    minimap.c: Game functions (mini-map, platforms, obstacles)

    header.h: Structures and prototypes

    minimap.h: Game-specific prototypes

@section build Compilation
bash

gcc -o game_complete main.c function.c minimap.c -lSDL2 -lSDL2_image -lSDL2_ttf -lSDL2_mixer -lm

./game_complete
